{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H3sRSAHmNRfrVGaRuizSts","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t# Who can change production: only the deploy workflow running in the \"production\" or\n     2\t# \"production-emergency\" GitHub environment can assume the deploy role, and both environments\n     3\t# require a named reviewer from agent-platform-leads. Nobody else has write access to the\n     4\t# clinic-agent namespace (see access_entries in main.tf), and the cluster API is private.\n     5\t\n     6\tprovider \"github\" {\n     7\t  owner = \"northbay-clinics\"\n     8\t}\n     9\t\n    10\tdata \"github_team\" \"leads\" {\n    11\t  slug = \"agent-platform-leads\"\n    12\t}\n    13\t\n    14\tresource \"github_branch_protection\" \"main\" {\n    15\t  repository_id = \"clinic-agent\"\n    16\t  pattern       = \"main\"\n    17\t\n    18\t  enforce_admins                  = true\n    19\t  allows_force_pushes             = false\n    20\t  allows_deletions                = false\n    21\t  required_linear_history         = true\n    22\t  require_signed_commits          = true\n    23\t  require_conversation_resolution = true\n    24\t\n    25\t  required_pull_request_reviews {\n    26\t    required_approving_review_count = 2\n    27\t    require_code_owner_reviews      = true\n    28\t    dismiss_stale_reviews           = true\n    29\t    require_last_push_approval      = true\n    30\t  }\n    31\t\n    32\t  required_status_checks {\n    33\t    strict   = true\n    34\t    contexts = [\"ci / test\", \"ci / manifest-check\"]\n    35\t  }\n    36\t}\n    37\t\n    38\tresource \"github_repository_environment\" \"production\" {\n    39\t  repository  = \"clinic-agent\"\n    40\t  environment = \"production\"\n    41\t  reviewers {\n    42\t    teams = [data.github_team.leads.id]\n    43\t  }\n    44\t  prevent_self_review = true\n    45\t  deployment_branch_policy {\n    46\t    protected_branches     = true\n    47\t    custom_branch_policies = false\n    48\t  }\n    49\t}\n    50\t\n    51\tresource \"github_repository_environment\" \"production_emergency\" {\n    52\t  repository  = \"clinic-agent\"\n    53\t  environment = \"production-emergency\"\n    54\t  reviewers {\n    55\t    teams = [data.github_team.leads.id]\n    56\t  }\n    57\t  prevent_self_review = true\n    58\t  deployment_branch_policy {\n    59\t    protected_branches     = false\n    60\t    custom_branch_policies = true\n    61\t  }\n    62\t}\n    63\t\n    64\tresource \"github_repository_environment_deployment_policy\" \"emergency_branches\" {\n    65\t  repository     = \"clinic-agent\"\n    66\t  environment    = github_repository_environment.production_emergency.environment\n    67\t  branch_pattern = \"hotfix/*\"\n    68\t}\n    69\t\n    70\tresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"deploy\" {\n    71\t  name = \"clinic-agent-deploy\"\n    72\t  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    73\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    74\t    Statement = [{\n    75\t      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n    76\t      Principal = { Federated = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:oidc-provider/token.actions.githubusercontent.com\" }\n    77\t      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\"\n    78\t      Condition = {\n    79\t        StringEquals = {\n    80\t          \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:aud\" = \"sts.amazonaws.com\"\n    81\t          \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub\" = [\n    82\t            \"repo:northbay-clinics/clinic-agent:environment:production\",\n    83\t            \"repo:northbay-clinics/clinic-agent:environment:production-emergency\",\n    84\t          ]\n    85\t        }\n    86\t      }\n    87\t    }]\n    88\t  })\n    89\t}\n    90\t\n    91\tresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"deploy\" {\n    92\t  name = \"clinic-agent-deploy\"\n    93\t  role = aws_iam_role.deploy.id\n    94\t  policy = jsonencode({\n    95\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    96\t    Statement = [\n    97\t      {\n    98\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n    99\t        Action   = [\"ecr:GetAuthorizationToken\"]\n   100\t        Resource = \"*\"\n   101\t      },\n   102\t      {\n   103\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n   104\t        Action   = [\"ecr:BatchCheckLayerAvailability\", \"ecr:PutImage\", \"ecr:InitiateLayerUpload\", \"ecr:UploadLayerPart\", \"ecr:CompleteLayerUpload\", \"ecr:BatchGetImage\"]\n   105\t        Resource = aws_ecr_repository.agent.arn\n   106\t      },\n   107\t      {\n   108\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n   109\t        Action   = [\"eks:DescribeCluster\"]\n   110\t        Resource = module.eks.cluster_arn\n   111\t      },\n   112\t    ]\n   113\t  })\n   114\t}\n50:      principal_arn = aws_iam_role.deploy.arn\n153:    role_arn            = aws_iam_role.firehose.arn\n     1\timport { DynamoDBClient } from \"@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb\";\n     2\timport { DynamoDBDocumentClient, GetCommand, PutCommand } from \"@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb\";\n     3\timport { createHash, randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\n     4\timport { env, policy } from \"../config.js\";\n     5\t\n     6\t// Staff approvals for high-impact tools. The agent creates a pending request; a front-desk lead or\n     7\t// clinic manager approves it in the staff console (which writes status, approvedBy, approverRole,\n     8\t// approvedAt); the agent then retries the tool with the approval id.\n     9\t\n    10\texport interface ApprovalRecord {\n    11\t  id: string;\n    12\t  status: \"pending\" | \"approved\" | \"rejected\";\n    13\t  tool: string;\n    14\t  tenantId: string;\n    15\t  agentInstanceId: string;\n    16\t  runId: string;\n    17\t  argsHash: string;\n    18\t  summary: string;\n    19\t  requestedAt: string;\n    20\t  expiresAt: string;\n    21\t  approvedBy?: string;\n    22\t  approverRole?: string;\n    23\t  approvedAt?: string;\n    24\t}\n    25\t\n    26\tconst ddb = DynamoDBDocumentClient.from(new DynamoDBClient({ region: env.region }));\n    27\t\n    28\texport function hashArgs(args: Record<string, unknown>): string {\n    29\t  const canonical = JSON.stringify(args, Object.keys(args).sort());\n    30\t  return createHash(\"sha256\").update(canonical).digest(\"hex\");\n    31\t}\n    32\t\n    33\texport async function requestApproval(req: {\n    34\t  tool: string;\n    35\t  tenantId: string;\n    36\t  agentInstanceId: string;\n    37\t  runId: string;\n    38\t  args: Record<string, unknown>;\n    39\t  summary: string;\n    40\t}): Promise<ApprovalRecord> {\n    41\t  const now = Date.now();\n    42\t  const rec: ApprovalRecord = {\n    43\t    id: randomUUID(),\n    44\t    status: \"pending\",\n    45\t    tool: req.tool,\n    46\t    tenantId: req.tenantId,\n    47\t    agentInstanceId: req.agentInstanceId,\n    48\t    runId: req.runId,\n    49\t    argsHash: hashArgs(req.args),\n    50\t    summary: req.summary,\n    51\t    requestedAt: new Date(now).toISOString(),\n    52\t    expiresAt: new Date(now + policy.approval.ttlSeconds * 1000).toISOString(),\n    53\t  };\n    54\t  await ddb.send(new PutCommand({ TableName: policy.approval.table, Item: rec, ConditionExpression: \"attribute_not_exists(id)\" }));\n    55\t  return rec;\n    56\t}\n    57\t\n    58\texport type ApprovalCheck = { ok: true; approval: ApprovalRecord } | { ok: false; reason: string };\n    59\t\n    60\texport async function checkApproval(req: {\n    61\t  approvalId: string;\n    62\t  tool: string;\n    63\t  tenantId: string;\n    64\t  args: Record<string, unknown>;\n    65\t}): Promise<ApprovalCheck> {\n    66\t  let rec: ApprovalRecord | undefined;\n    67\t  try {\n    68\t    const res = await ddb.send(new GetCommand({ TableName: policy.approval.table, Key: { id: req.approvalId }, ConsistentRead: true }));\n    69\t    rec = res.Item as ApprovalRecord | undefined;\n    70\t  } catch (err) {\n    71\t    return { ok: false, reason: `approval store unavailable: ${(err as Error).message}` };\n    72\t  }\n    73\t  if (!rec) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval not found\" };\n    74\t  if (rec.status !== \"approved\") return { ok: false, reason: `approval is ${rec.status}` };\n    75\t  if (rec.tool !== req.tool) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval is for a different tool\" };\n    76\t  if (rec.tenantId !== req.tenantId) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval is for a different clinic\" };\n    77\t  if (Date.parse(rec.expiresAt) <= Date.now()) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval expired\" };\n    78\t  if (!rec.approverRole || !policy.approval.approverRoles.includes(rec.approverRole)) {\n    79\t    return { ok: false, reason: \"approver lacks authority\" };\n    80\t  }\n    81\t  return { ok: true, approval: rec };\n    82\t}\nname: deploy\n\n# Deploys the image digest named in release/manifest.json. The digest reaches the manifest through\n# a reviewed release PR, so what runs is always a reviewed commit.\non:\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      emergency:\n        description: Emergency change (hotfix/* branch, production-emergency environment)\n        type: boolean\n        default: false\n      owner:\n        description: Emergency only - person accountable for this change\n        type: string\n        default: \"\"\n      reason:\n        description: Emergency only - why this cannot wait for a normal release\n        type: string\n        default: \"\"\n      expires_on:\n        description: Emergency only - date (YYYY-MM-DD) by which it is replaced by a normal release\n        type: string\n        default: \"\"\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n  id-token: write\n  issues: write\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: deploy-production\n  cancel-in-progress: false\n\njobs:\n  deploy:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    environment: ${{ inputs.emergency && 'production-emergency' || 'production' }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@08eba0b27e820071cde6df949e0beb9ba4906955 # v4.3.0\n\n      - name: Emergency change record is complete\n        if: inputs.emergency\n        env:\n          OWNER: ${{ inputs.owner }}\n          REASON: ${{ inputs.reason }}\n          EXPIRES_ON: ${{ inputs.expires_on }}\n        run: |\n          test -n \"$OWNER\" || { echo \"owner is required\"; exit 1; }\n          test -n \"$REASON\" || { echo \"reason is required\"; exit 1; }\n          date -d \"$EXPIRES_ON\" +%F >/dev/null || { echo \"expires_on must be a date\"; exit 1; }\n          [[ \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\" == hotfix/* ]] || { echo \"emergency deploys come from hotfix/* branches\"; exit 1; }\n\n      - uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@a03048d87541d1d9fcf2ecf528a4a65ba9bd7838 # v5.0.0\n        with:\n          role-to-assume: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-deploy\n          aws-region: us-west-2\n\n      - uses: sigstore/cosign-installer@d58896d6a1865668819e1d91763c7751a165e159 # v3.9.2\n        with:\n          cosign-release: v2.6.2\n\n      - name: Verify image signature\n        run: |\n          DIGEST=$(jq -r .image.digest release/manifest.json)\n          REPO=$(jq -r .image.repository release/manifest.json)\n          cosign verify \"$REPO@$DIGEST\" \\\n            --certificate-identity \"https://github.com/northbay-clinics/clinic-agent/.github/workflows/ci.yml@refs/heads/main\" \\\n            --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\n          grep -q \"$DIGEST\" k8s/deployment.yaml || { echo \"k8s/deployment.yaml does not use the manifest digest\"; exit 1; }\n\n      - name: Apply\n        run: |\n          aws eks update-kubeconfig --name clinic-agent-prod\n          kubectl apply -f k8s/deployment.yaml\n          kubectl -n clinic-agent annotate deployment/clinic-agent --overwrite \\\n            northbay.example/git-sha=\"$GITHUB_SHA\" \\\n            northbay.example/release=\"$(jq -r .release release/manifest.json)\" \\\n            northbay.example/deployed-by=\"$GITHUB_ACTOR\" \\\n            northbay.example/run=\"$GITHUB_SERVER_URL/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/actions/runs/$GITHUB_RUN_ID\"\n          kubectl -n clinic-agent rollout status deployment/clinic-agent --timeout=5m\n\n      - name: Open follow-up review for emergency change\n        if: inputs.emergency\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n          OWNER: ${{ inputs.owner }}\n          REASON: ${{ inputs.reason }}\n          EXPIRES_ON: ${{ inputs.expires_on }}\n        run: |\n          gh issue create \\\n            --title \"Follow-up review: emergency deploy ${GITHUB_SHA::8}\" \\\n            --label emergency-change,needs-review \\\n            --assignee \"$OWNER\" \\\n            --body \"Owner: $OWNER\n          Reason: $REASON\n          Ends: $EXPIRES_ON\n          Commit: $GITHUB_SHA\n          Approved in environment production-emergency by a required reviewer (see run $GITHUB_RUN_ID).\n          Review and merge to main via normal PR before the end date.\"\n# clinic-agent\n\nPatient-scheduling agent for the Northbay Clinic Group. Patients reach it by SMS or by the web chat\nwidget on each clinic's site. It looks up, books, reschedules, and cancels appointments in the EHR,\nsends SMS reminders, refunds no-show deposits, and asks the insurance-eligibility agent whether a\nvisit is covered.\n\nEach clinic is a tenant. A clinic's patients, appointments, deposits, and EHR credentials are kept\nseparate from every other clinic's.\n\n## Components\n\n| Piece | Where | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| HTTP service (Fastify) | `src/server.ts` | `/v1/sms/inbound` webhook, `/v1/chat` web chat |\n| Agent loop | `src/agent/loop.ts` | Claude Sonnet 4.5 snapshot, tool use |\n| Intent classifier | `src/agent/classifier.ts` | Claude Haiku 4.5 snapshot, routes emergencies and complaints to staff |\n| Tool registry | `src/tools/registry.ts` | EHR MCP server plus native tools, scanned on load |\n| Tool executor | `src/tools/executor.ts` | allowlist, kill switch, budgets, approvals, audit |\n| EHR | `src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` | MCP over streamable HTTP with mTLS, per-clinic OAuth client |\n| Payments | `src/integrations/payments.ts` | deposit refunds, provider idempotency keys |\n| SMS | `src/integrations/sms.ts` | outbound reminders and replies |\n| Eligibility peer | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` | A2A `message/send`, token exchange per call |\n| Reminder job | `src/workers/reminders.ts` | Kubernetes CronJob, 17:00 local each day |\n\nThere is no vector store and no conversation memory. Every run starts from the patient's message and\nthe EHR. Conversation transcripts are not stored by this service.\n\n## High-impact actions\n\n`config/policy.yaml` lists the tools that need a staff approval before they run. The agent asks for\nthe approval, a front-desk lead or clinic manager approves it in the staff console, and the agent\nretries with the approval ID. Approvals expire after 15 minutes.\n\n## Stopping the agent\n\nOperators with the `clinic-agent-ops` role set `halted = true` on the `global` item (all clinics) or a\n`tenant#<clinicId>` item in the `clinic-agent-control` DynamoDB table:\n\n```bash\naws dynamodb put-item --table-name clinic-agent-control \\\n  --item '{\"pk\":{\"S\":\"global\"},\"halted\":{\"BOOL\":true},\"by\":{\"S\":\"<you>\"}}'\n```\n\nRunning work checks the flag before each model turn and each tool call, and a watcher aborts in-flight\nrequests within 2 seconds.\n\n## Identity\n\n`src/agent/identity.ts` computes the agent-type-id from the image digest, harness version, prompts,\nmodel IDs, and config. Each pod also gets a random agent-instance-id at start. Both are on every\naudit record together with the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, and trace context.\n\n## Build and test\n\n```bash\nnpm ci\nnpm run lint\nnpm test\nnpm run build","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3501af70-8e84-4308-8a18-dd718bb57490","uuid":"1dcec6fc-4903-4d75-91a7-44e0db627949","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:34:00.452Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     1\t# Who can change production: only the deploy workflow running in the \"production\" or\n     2\t# \"production-emergency\" GitHub environment can assume the deploy role, and both environments\n     3\t# require a named reviewer from agent-platform-leads. Nobody else has write access to the\n     4\t# clinic-agent namespace (see access_entries in main.tf), and the cluster API is private.\n     5\t\n     6\tprovider \"github\" {\n     7\t  owner = \"northbay-clinics\"\n     8\t}\n     9\t\n    10\tdata \"github_team\" \"leads\" {\n    11\t  slug = \"agent-platform-leads\"\n    12\t}\n    13\t\n    14\tresource \"github_branch_protection\" \"main\" {\n    15\t  repository_id = \"clinic-agent\"\n    16\t  pattern       = \"main\"\n    17\t\n    18\t  enforce_admins                  = true\n    19\t  allows_force_pushes             = false\n    20\t  allows_deletions                = false\n    21\t  required_linear_history         = true\n    22\t  require_signed_commits          = true\n    23\t  require_conversation_resolution = true\n    24\t\n    25\t  required_pull_request_reviews {\n    26\t    required_approving_review_count = 2\n    27\t    require_code_owner_reviews      = true\n    28\t    dismiss_stale_reviews           = true\n    29\t    require_last_push_approval      = true\n    30\t  }\n    31\t\n    32\t  required_status_checks {\n    33\t    strict   = true\n    34\t    contexts = [\"ci / test\", \"ci / manifest-check\"]\n    35\t  }\n    36\t}\n    37\t\n    38\tresource \"github_repository_environment\" \"production\" {\n    39\t  repository  = \"clinic-agent\"\n    40\t  environment = \"production\"\n    41\t  reviewers {\n    42\t    teams = [data.github_team.leads.id]\n    43\t  }\n    44\t  prevent_self_review = true\n    45\t  deployment_branch_policy {\n    46\t    protected_branches     = true\n    47\t    custom_branch_policies = false\n    48\t  }\n    49\t}\n    50\t\n    51\tresource \"github_repository_environment\" \"production_emergency\" {\n    52\t  repository  = \"clinic-agent\"\n    53\t  environment = \"production-emergency\"\n    54\t  reviewers {\n    55\t    teams = [data.github_team.leads.id]\n    56\t  }\n    57\t  prevent_self_review = true\n    58\t  deployment_branch_policy {\n    59\t    protected_branches     = false\n    60\t    custom_branch_policies = true\n    61\t  }\n    62\t}\n    63\t\n    64\tresource \"github_repository_environment_deployment_policy\" \"emergency_branches\" {\n    65\t  repository     = \"clinic-agent\"\n    66\t  environment    = github_repository_environment.production_emergency.environment\n    67\t  branch_pattern = \"hotfix/*\"\n    68\t}\n    69\t\n    70\tresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"deploy\" {\n    71\t  name = \"clinic-agent-deploy\"\n    72\t  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    73\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    74\t    Statement = [{\n    75\t      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n    76\t      Principal = { Federated = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:oidc-provider/token.actions.githubusercontent.com\" }\n    77\t      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\"\n    78\t      Condition = {\n    79\t        StringEquals = {\n    80\t          \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:aud\" = \"sts.amazonaws.com\"\n    81\t          \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub\" = [\n    82\t            \"repo:northbay-clinics/clinic-agent:environment:production\",\n    83\t            \"repo:northbay-clinics/clinic-agent:environment:production-emergency\",\n    84\t          ]\n    85\t        }\n    86\t      }\n    87\t    }]\n    88\t  })\n    89\t}\n    90\t\n    91\tresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"deploy\" {\n    92\t  name = \"clinic-agent-deploy\"\n    93\t  role = aws_iam_role.deploy.id\n    94\t  policy = jsonencode({\n    95\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    96\t    Statement = [\n    97\t      {\n    98\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n    99\t        Action   = [\"ecr:GetAuthorizationToken\"]\n   100\t        Resource = \"*\"\n   101\t      },\n   102\t      {\n   103\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n   104\t        Action   = [\"ecr:BatchCheckLayerAvailability\", \"ecr:PutImage\", \"ecr:InitiateLayerUpload\", \"ecr:UploadLayerPart\", \"ecr:CompleteLayerUpload\", \"ecr:BatchGetImage\"]\n   105\t        Resource = aws_ecr_repository.agent.arn\n   106\t      },\n   107\t      {\n   108\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n   109\t        Action   = [\"eks:DescribeCluster\"]\n   110\t        Resource = module.eks.cluster_arn\n   111\t      },\n   112\t    ]\n   113\t  })\n   114\t}\n50:      principal_arn = aws_iam_role.deploy.arn\n153:    role_arn            = aws_iam_role.firehose.arn\n     1\timport { DynamoDBClient } from \"@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb\";\n     2\timport { DynamoDBDocumentClient, GetCommand, PutCommand } from \"@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb\";\n     3\timport { createHash, randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\n     4\timport { env, policy } from \"../config.js\";\n     5\t\n     6\t// Staff approvals for high-impact tools. The agent creates a pending request; a front-desk lead or\n     7\t// clinic manager approves it in the staff console (which writes status, approvedBy, approverRole,\n     8\t// approvedAt); the agent then retries the tool with the approval id.\n     9\t\n    10\texport interface ApprovalRecord {\n    11\t  id: string;\n    12\t  status: \"pending\" | \"approved\" | \"rejected\";\n    13\t  tool: string;\n    14\t  tenantId: string;\n    15\t  agentInstanceId: string;\n    16\t  runId: string;\n    17\t  argsHash: string;\n    18\t  summary: string;\n    19\t  requestedAt: string;\n    20\t  expiresAt: string;\n    21\t  approvedBy?: string;\n    22\t  approverRole?: string;\n    23\t  approvedAt?: string;\n    24\t}\n    25\t\n    26\tconst ddb = DynamoDBDocumentClient.from(new DynamoDBClient({ region: env.region }));\n    27\t\n    28\texport function hashArgs(args: Record<string, unknown>): string {\n    29\t  const canonical = JSON.stringify(args, Object.keys(args).sort());\n    30\t  return createHash(\"sha256\").update(canonical).digest(\"hex\");\n    31\t}\n    32\t\n    33\texport async function requestApproval(req: {\n    34\t  tool: string;\n    35\t  tenantId: string;\n    36\t  agentInstanceId: string;\n    37\t  runId: string;\n    38\t  args: Record<string, unknown>;\n    39\t  summary: string;\n    40\t}): Promise<ApprovalRecord> {\n    41\t  const now = Date.now();\n    42\t  const rec: ApprovalRecord = {\n    43\t    id: randomUUID(),\n    44\t    status: \"pending\",\n    45\t    tool: req.tool,\n    46\t    tenantId: req.tenantId,\n    47\t    agentInstanceId: req.agentInstanceId,\n    48\t    runId: req.runId,\n    49\t    argsHash: hashArgs(req.args),\n    50\t    summary: req.summary,\n    51\t    requestedAt: new Date(now).toISOString(),\n    52\t    expiresAt: new Date(now + policy.approval.ttlSeconds * 1000).toISOString(),\n    53\t  };\n    54\t  await ddb.send(new PutCommand({ TableName: policy.approval.table, Item: rec, ConditionExpression: \"attribute_not_exists(id)\" }));\n    55\t  return rec;\n    56\t}\n    57\t\n    58\texport type ApprovalCheck = { ok: true; approval: ApprovalRecord } | { ok: false; reason: string };\n    59\t\n    60\texport async function checkApproval(req: {\n    61\t  approvalId: string;\n    62\t  tool: string;\n    63\t  tenantId: string;\n    64\t  args: Record<string, unknown>;\n    65\t}): Promise<ApprovalCheck> {\n    66\t  let rec: ApprovalRecord | undefined;\n    67\t  try {\n    68\t    const res = await ddb.send(new GetCommand({ TableName: policy.approval.table, Key: { id: req.approvalId }, ConsistentRead: true }));\n    69\t    rec = res.Item as ApprovalRecord | undefined;\n    70\t  } catch (err) {\n    71\t    return { ok: false, reason: `approval store unavailable: ${(err as Error).message}` };\n    72\t  }\n    73\t  if (!rec) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval not found\" };\n    74\t  if (rec.status !== \"approved\") return { ok: false, reason: `approval is ${rec.status}` };\n    75\t  if (rec.tool !== req.tool) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval is for a different tool\" };\n    76\t  if (rec.tenantId !== req.tenantId) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval is for a different clinic\" };\n    77\t  if (Date.parse(rec.expiresAt) <= Date.now()) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval expired\" };\n    78\t  if (!rec.approverRole || !policy.approval.approverRoles.includes(rec.approverRole)) {\n    79\t    return { ok: false, reason: \"approver lacks authority\" };\n    80\t  }\n    81\t  return { ok: true, approval: rec };\n    82\t}\nname: deploy\n\n# Deploys the image digest named in release/manifest.json. The digest reaches the manifest through\n# a reviewed release PR, so what runs is always a reviewed commit.\non:\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      emergency:\n        description: Emergency change (hotfix/* branch, production-emergency environment)\n        type: boolean\n        default: false\n      owner:\n        description: Emergency only - person accountable for this change\n        type: string\n        default: \"\"\n      reason:\n        description: Emergency only - why this cannot wait for a normal release\n        type: string\n        default: \"\"\n      expires_on:\n        description: Emergency only - date (YYYY-MM-DD) by which it is replaced by a normal release\n        type: string\n        default: \"\"\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n  id-token: write\n  issues: write\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: deploy-production\n  cancel-in-progress: false\n\njobs:\n  deploy:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    environment: ${{ inputs.emergency && 'production-emergency' || 'production' }}\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@08eba0b27e820071cde6df949e0beb9ba4906955 # v4.3.0\n\n      - name: Emergency change record is complete\n        if: inputs.emergency\n        env:\n          OWNER: ${{ inputs.owner }}\n          REASON: ${{ inputs.reason }}\n          EXPIRES_ON: ${{ inputs.expires_on }}\n        run: |\n          test -n \"$OWNER\" || { echo \"owner is required\"; exit 1; }\n          test -n \"$REASON\" || { echo \"reason is required\"; exit 1; }\n          date -d \"$EXPIRES_ON\" +%F >/dev/null || { echo \"expires_on must be a date\"; exit 1; }\n          [[ \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\" == hotfix/* ]] || { echo \"emergency deploys come from hotfix/* branches\"; exit 1; }\n\n      - uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@a03048d87541d1d9fcf2ecf528a4a65ba9bd7838 # v5.0.0\n        with:\n          role-to-assume: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-deploy\n          aws-region: us-west-2\n\n      - uses: sigstore/cosign-installer@d58896d6a1865668819e1d91763c7751a165e159 # v3.9.2\n        with:\n          cosign-release: v2.6.2\n\n      - name: Verify image signature\n        run: |\n          DIGEST=$(jq -r .image.digest release/manifest.json)\n          REPO=$(jq -r .image.repository release/manifest.json)\n          cosign verify \"$REPO@$DIGEST\" \\\n            --certificate-identity \"https://github.com/northbay-clinics/clinic-agent/.github/workflows/ci.yml@refs/heads/main\" \\\n            --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\n          grep -q \"$DIGEST\" k8s/deployment.yaml || { echo \"k8s/deployment.yaml does not use the manifest digest\"; exit 1; }\n\n      - name: Apply\n        run: |\n          aws eks update-kubeconfig --name clinic-agent-prod\n          kubectl apply -f k8s/deployment.yaml\n          kubectl -n clinic-agent annotate deployment/clinic-agent --overwrite \\\n            northbay.example/git-sha=\"$GITHUB_SHA\" \\\n            northbay.example/release=\"$(jq -r .release release/manifest.json)\" \\\n            northbay.example/deployed-by=\"$GITHUB_ACTOR\" \\\n            northbay.example/run=\"$GITHUB_SERVER_URL/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/actions/runs/$GITHUB_RUN_ID\"\n          kubectl -n clinic-agent rollout status deployment/clinic-agent --timeout=5m\n\n      - name: Open follow-up review for emergency change\n        if: inputs.emergency\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n          OWNER: ${{ inputs.owner }}\n          REASON: ${{ inputs.reason }}\n          EXPIRES_ON: ${{ inputs.expires_on }}\n        run: |\n          gh issue create \\\n            --title \"Follow-up review: emergency deploy ${GITHUB_SHA::8}\" \\\n            --label emergency-change,needs-review \\\n            --assignee \"$OWNER\" \\\n            --body \"Owner: $OWNER\n          Reason: $REASON\n          Ends: $EXPIRES_ON\n          Commit: $GITHUB_SHA\n          Approved in environment production-emergency by a required reviewer (see run $GITHUB_RUN_ID).\n          Review and merge to main via normal PR before the end date.\"\n# clinic-agent\n\nPatient-scheduling agent for the Northbay Clinic Group. Patients reach it by SMS or by the web chat\nwidget on each clinic's site. It looks up, books, reschedules, and cancels appointments in the EHR,\nsends SMS reminders, refunds no-show deposits, and asks the insurance-eligibility agent whether a\nvisit is covered.\n\nEach clinic is a tenant. A clinic's patients, appointments, deposits, and EHR credentials are kept\nseparate from every other clinic's.\n\n## Components\n\n| Piece | Where | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| HTTP service (Fastify) | `src/server.ts` | `/v1/sms/inbound` webhook, `/v1/chat` web chat |\n| Agent loop | `src/agent/loop.ts` | Claude Sonnet 4.5 snapshot, tool use |\n| Intent classifier | `src/agent/classifier.ts` | Claude Haiku 4.5 snapshot, routes emergencies and complaints to staff |\n| Tool registry | `src/tools/registry.ts` | EHR MCP server plus native tools, scanned on load |\n| Tool executor | `src/tools/executor.ts` | allowlist, kill switch, budgets, approvals, audit |\n| EHR | `src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` | MCP over streamable HTTP with mTLS, per-clinic OAuth client |\n| Payments | `src/integrations/payments.ts` | deposit refunds, provider idempotency keys |\n| SMS | `src/integrations/sms.ts` | outbound reminders and replies |\n| Eligibility peer | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` | A2A `message/send`, token exchange per call |\n| Reminder job | `src/workers/reminders.ts` | Kubernetes CronJob, 17:00 local each day |\n\nThere is no vector store and no conversation memory. Every run starts from the patient's message and\nthe EHR. Conversation transcripts are not stored by this service.\n\n## High-impact actions\n\n`config/policy.yaml` lists the tools that need a staff approval before they run. The agent asks for\nthe approval, a front-desk lead or clinic manager approves it in the staff console, and the agent\nretries with the approval ID. Approvals expire after 15 minutes.\n\n## Stopping the agent\n\nOperators with the `clinic-agent-ops` role set `halted = true` on the `global` item (all clinics) or a\n`tenant#<clinicId>` item in the `clinic-agent-control` DynamoDB table:\n\n```bash\naws dynamodb put-item --table-name clinic-agent-control \\\n  --item '{\"pk\":{\"S\":\"global\"},\"halted\":{\"BOOL\":true},\"by\":{\"S\":\"<you>\"}}'\n```\n\nRunning work checks the flag before each model turn and each tool call, and a watcher aborts in-flight\nrequests within 2 seconds.\n\n## Identity\n\n`src/agent/identity.ts` computes the agent-type-id from the image digest, harness version, prompts,\nmodel IDs, and config. Each pod also gets a random agent-instance-id at start. Both are on every\naudit record together with the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, and trace context.\n\n## Build and test\n\n```bash\nnpm ci\nnpm run lint\nnpm test\nnpm run build","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01H3sRSAHmNRfrVGaRuizSts","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
