{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDVxoyvc8t3wtJmX4dDx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed R14, A01, A02, A03 and A04 and saved the results in `agent/brace-findings.json`. It passes `validate_findings.py --batch R14,A01,A02,A03,A04 --before-challenges --fix` with 4 gaps and 1 na_candidate. I didn't run challenges, as you asked, so every rating is unchallenged.\n\n- **A01 (gap):** EHR and payments calls use static per-clinic secrets (`src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:41`, `src/integrations/payments.ts:33`). The agent and reminders service accounts share one IAM role (`k8s/deployment.yaml:27`). The patient is only a scope string in the eligibility token exchange (`src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:44`).\n- **A02 (gap):** Refusals before a run starts (webchat 401/400/404, SMS 400/404) write no audit record. A failed SMS signature is only logged (`src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:51`). Tenant comes from the `x-clinic-id` header (`src/routes/webchat.ts:43`). The audit schema itself has all six fields, and the trace context is stored in the record.\n- **A03 (gap):** The type-id hash only reads `prompts/*.txt` (`src/agent/identity.ts:24`), so `prompts/system.md` is not hashed. The model IDs are pinned snapshots, the ordering is fixed, and no secrets enter the manifest.\n- **A04 (gap):** Tenant comes from the model's `clinicId` tool argument (`src/tools/executor.ts:63`), the `x-clinic-id` header, and the SMS body even when its signature fails. The approval handoff carries no trace context (`src/tools/approvals.ts:42`). A02 and A04 list each other in `also_affects`.\n- **R14 (na_candidate):** No checkpoints, replay log or recovery from audit records exist. Audit is write-only to Firehose. The only retry is the SDK's single model-call retry (`src/agent/loop.ts:15`).\n  - I set the R14 evidence entry by editing the JSON, because `answer.py` only derives item evidence from yes/no checks.\n  - R14.1–R14.5 are left as unknown, since checks on an na_candidate item don't count.\n- **Prescan hits:** All 11 belong to B11, B02, R13 and E03, so none are resolved here. Say so if you want H005 (the wildcard IAM resource) dismissed under A01.\n- **Notes:** The scope in the file says this was a partial-batch review. I found no injection attempts.\n- **Helper files:** The ledger helper files are in `ledgers/` at the workspace root. I also generated `brace-inventory.json` and `brace-prescan.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":696,"cache_read_input_tokens":90257,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":696},"output_tokens":823,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3501af70-8e84-4308-8a18-dd718bb57490","uuid":"83d7e7c9-f71f-47b1-805f-7cc7b2277da6","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:36:56.574Z","request_id":"req_011CgDVxoacsYpUrF9TD2kJL"}
